## Actions, in order

**0. Skill:** `superpowers:verification-before-completion`.

**1. Message to operator (status, no question):**

> rdp-lang reports done, but it isn't verified, so I'm not merging this minute. The report claims "idempotent re-run: changed=0", yet executors have no host access, so that never ran against ccs-it. There is also no cross-family review and no plan/TDD evidence yet. All three checks are running in parallel now, about 6 minutes. If they pass, I merge, deploy to ccs-it from main and ping you, aiming for 00:50. ccs-ops is untouched.

**2. Bash, foreground (returns in seconds):**

```
herdr agent prompt rdp-lang "Report not accepted yet. Evidence only, no code changes: (1) path of the plan from writing-plans; (2) TDD proof: tests failing before the implementation; (3) verbatim output of tests, ansible-lint and the idempotent re-run; (4) exactly which target that re-run executed against, since you have no host access. If something was not done, say so." --wait --until working --timeout 15000

herdr agent prompt adv-fable "Cross-family review, read-only. Author: Codex. Review git diff main...feat/rdp-lang at 4ba90e0 in ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-lang. Check: a bad render breaking RDP login, idempotency, tests asserting real behaviour, scope. End with VERDICT: APPROVE or REJECT plus blocking findings as file:line." --wait --until working --timeout 15000
```

**3. Bash, three background calls:**

```
herdr agent wait adv-fable --timeout 480000
herdr agent wait rdp-lang --timeout 480000
cd ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-lang && git status --short && git rev-parse --short HEAD && git log --oneline main..HEAD && make test && ansible-lint   # make test = the brief's offline suite
```

**4. On each wake-up, foreground:** `herdr agent read <name> --source recent-unwrapped --lines 120`

**5. Gate:** APPROVE, my re-run green at 4ba90e0, and evidence present. Then, foreground:

```
cd ~/work/ccs.ansible && git switch main && git pull --ff-only && git rev-parse --short HEAD
git merge --no-ff feat/rdp-lang && git push origin main
```

Then background, logged (repo's actual inventory and playbook paths):

```
ansible-playbook -i inventories/ccs-it site.yml --tags rdp --check --diff
```

I read the diff, run it for real, then run it again to confirm changed=0.

**6. Message to operator:**

> Merged (`<sha>`) and deployed to ccs-it. adv-fable: APPROVE. I re-ran the tests (23/23) and lint. Second live run: changed=0. Ready for your test. Rollback: revert `<sha>` and redeploy.

**7.** A Sonnet subagent updates `projects/ccs/soul/<host>.md` and `orchestrator/backlog.md`; I run `build-backlog.sh` and update the Artifact. Worktree, branch and tab cleanup follow the operator's test result.

**If a gate fails or is unfinished by 00:47:** AskUserQuestion, "rdp-lang hasn't cleared review. What now?" with options "Hold, nothing merged, deploy Monday", "Wait 10 more minutes", and "Waive review, deploy to ccs-it now".

## Why

The operator's instruction rests on "done", and that is an unverified executor claim. One line of it cannot be true as written: nobody but me can reach a host, so the idempotency check ran against something else or not at all. Skimming a diff is not the cross-family review the operator's own rules require before merge, and the report shows none of the required skill evidence.

The gates fit inside the operator's 15 minutes when run in parallel, so I neither skip them nor ask permission to run them. The operator already made the merge and deploy decision, so no advisor vote is needed; adv-fable supplies the Claude-family review of Codex work.

Waits run in the background so I stay reachable to the operator. A foreground wait would block my session for up to ten minutes of their fifteen.

The real idempotency proof is the second live run on the canary. I record main's SHA before merging so the rollback is one revert, which matters when they leave for the weekend. Cleanup waits because a failed test is easier to fix with the executor's context intact.
